window.docContents[216].resolve({"/Elliptic-Equations/Coverage-and-Open-Problems/#PDEAtlas--Elliptic-Equations--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Elliptic-Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Regularity-and-geometry--Operational-boundary-geometry":{"contents":"Global Dirichlet regularity uses an operational atlas: finite interior and\nboundary cutoffs, flattening charts, inverse charts, differentiability data,\nbounded targets, and the identities needed to transport the equation. A\nbounded open set whose boundary is locally a  graph, , has\nsuch an atlas with  charts and inverse charts.\n\nTwo concrete atlases are built by hand. The interval  has affine\nendpoint charts, and every positive-dimensional Euclidean unit ball has a\nfinite signed-cap cover, a subordinate partition of unity, globally smooth\nheight extensions, and complete graph-flattening charts. Both supply the charts required by global boundary regularity.\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Elliptic Equations\u0009Coverage and Open Problems\u0009Elliptic Coverage and Open Problems\u0009Regularity and geometry","header":"5.7.1.3.2. Operational boundary geometry","id":"/Elliptic-Equations/Coverage-and-Open-Problems/#PDEAtlas--Elliptic-Equations--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Elliptic-Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Regularity-and-geometry--Operational-boundary-geometry"},"/Parabolic-Equations/Coverage-and-Open-Problems/#PDEAtlas--Parabolic-Equations--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Classical-and-Weak-Heat-Flow--Nonlinear-diffusion-and-reaction":{"contents":"Convex gradient diffusion () has a\nglobal weak Dirichlet solution from  data on bounded \ngraph domains, for  uniformly convex densities with bounded Hessian.\nTuring instability () is proved for\nthe linear two-species system from the raw coefficient inequalities. For a\nconvex reaction dominating a superlinear power, the weak nonlinear heat\nequation on a bounded connected domain has no nonnegative solution up to a\nprescribed time once the initial eigenfunction moment exceeds an explicit\nsufficient threshold ().\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Parabolic Equations\u0009Coverage and Open Problems\u0009Classical and Weak Heat Flow","header":"6.8.1.3. Nonlinear diffusion and reaction","id":"/Parabolic-Equations/Coverage-and-Open-Problems/#PDEAtlas--Parabolic-Equations--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Classical-and-Weak-Heat-Flow--Nonlinear-diffusion-and-reaction"},"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/Coverage-and-Open-Problems/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Sobolev-Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Fourier-and-fractional-Sobolev-theory":{"contents":"For every real , we use Mathlib's complex Hilbert space H^{s}(ℝ^n)\nof tempered distributions. Three representatives are kept separate.\n\n1. toLp u represents the Bessel potential\n.2. 𝓕 (toLp u) is the Fourier transform of that  representative.3. For , toL2Fun is the physical  representative of\n itself.\n\nThe third object need not exist at negative order.  This is why the carrier\nremains a space of distributions rather than being forced into an \nfunction model.\n\nThe whole-space theory contains:\n\n* the exact norm identity through the weighted Fourier representative;* the isometric equivalence between each  and complex ;* scale inclusions  for ;* Bessel-potential shifts between arbitrary real orders;* weak coordinate derivatives ;* a single canonical real physical subspace HsSpaceReal, realized as a\nclosed and complete kernel;* Hermitian-symmetry characterizations of real-valuedness;* a continuous real-linear equivalence\n for natural ;* explicit forward and reverse norm bounds for that integer bridge;* for  and , the whole-space Gagliardo seminorm identity\nwith its named positive kernel constant, together with the corresponding\nFourier-side finiteness criterion; and* a continuous real-linear equivalence between the completed whole-space\nGagliardoSpace and , preserving the physical\n function, with explicit norm bounds in both directions.\n\nThere is a single physical carrier. Characterization theorems relate\nHsSpaceReal to toL2Fun, and the weak-derivative and integer-equivalence\nresults are all stated for this one space.\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Sobolev Spaces and Weak Derivatives\u0009Coverage and Open Problems\u0009Sobolev Coverage and Open Problems","header":"4.6.1.12. Fourier and fractional Sobolev theory","id":"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/Coverage-and-Open-Problems/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Sobolev-Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Fourier-and-fractional-Sobolev-theory"}});